ub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- 4.6.3.stable (confirmed bug)\n- Not tested on earlier versions yet\n\n\n### System information\n\nOS: Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Linux 6.17.0, x86_64   CPU: (Intel, architecture Alder Lake) GPU: Intel Iris Xe Graphics (Alder Lake-UP3) Rendering backend: GL Compatibility\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen running `godot --headless --export-debug \"Android\" out.apk` on x86_64 Linux with \na fully configured Android preset (valid SDK, JDK 21, keystore), the export fails with:\n\n  ERROR: Cannot export project with preset \"Android\" due to configuration errors:\n  [blank line — no error text]\n\nThe blank message makes it impossible to diagnose the issue from CLI.\n\nRoot cause: in platform/android/export/export_plugin.cpp, when \n`should_import_etc2_astc()` returns false (which it does on x86_64 Linux because \nthe preferred texture format is S3TC_BPTC, not ETC2_ASTC), the code sets \n`valid = false` but never appends a human-readable message to the error string `err`.\n\nWorkaround: add `textures/vram_compression/import_etc2_astc=true` under [rendering] \nin project.godot.\n\nFix needed: add the missing error message when valid is set to false for this reason.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new Godot 4.6 project on x86_64 Linux\n2. Configure an Android export preset (valid Android SDK, JDK, debug keystore)\n3. Do NOT enable \"Import ETC2 ASTC\" in Project Settings\n4. Run: godot --headless --export-debug \"Android\" /tmp/out.apk\n5. Observe: \"configuration errors:\" with blank message, no actionable info\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSteps: configure Android SDK + JDK in Editor Settings, then run:\n  godot --headless --export-debug \"Android\" /tmp/out.apk\nExpected: clear error about ETC2/ASTC\nActual: blank error message (single \\n)\n","closed_by":{